study.body:
What limits the power a line can carry depends on its length:
- short lines (up to about 80 km): the conductors' **thermal** rating;
- medium lines (about 80–320 km): the **voltage drop** (typically $V_R \geq 0.95V_S$);
- long lines: the **steady-state stability** limit. A lossless long line behaves like $X' = Z_c\sin\beta\ell$, so $P_{max} = \text{SIL}/\sin\beta\ell$ at rated voltages; in practice $\delta$ is kept below about 35° for margin.
